                            "archaic"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1bca43f3-648f-48cd-a96a-e19c1f0db593",
                                "sense_id": "f1e2c16d-1dfd-3053-a809-7a7f94961bed",
                                "text": "There are a very great many kinds of saugh, or willow tree, and Holland is said to be the native place, and great nursery of them"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "98aa1aef-23b7-4e73-97ab-82a96dc7068c",
                                "sense_id": "f1e2c16d-1dfd-3053-a809-7a7f94961bed",
                                "text": "After that we have cutte our wilfes and saughs[…]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "de7862f4-6bbc-4d90-8e97-d66c0b78cfc7",
                                "sense_id": "f1e2c16d-1dfd-3053-a809-7a7f94961bed",
                                "text": "There are some parts of Scotland where it would be impossible to find a saugh for miles that had not a grassy mound before it, telling a bloody tale."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2fa9b38d-cac4-374a-9393-449ab075d7d8",
                        "entry_id": "40a7df70-8232-30ba-bb23-d27b1af658b0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A small burn or creek."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "81050e38-9cdb-43ad-9627-4b9a0ba11769",
                                "sense_id": "2fa9b38d-cac4-374a-9393-449ab075d7d8",
                                "text": "By Morgany doe drive her through her watry saugh (marginal gloss) A kind of Trench."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ce9ac763-3958-4aa3-b6e4-6318b9558c3f",
                                "sense_id": "2fa9b38d-cac4-374a-9393-449ab075d7d8",
                                "text": "The nest, which is composed of dry bents lined with hair, is generally built close to the ground, among rank vegetation or rushes, but I have sometimes found it in low willow bushes in a saugh bog."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f1adfbaf-ed57-4f2e-b1aa-087c3c8a81f3",
                                "sense_id": "2fa9b38d-cac4-374a-9393-449ab075d7d8",
                                "text": "oo the lambies bleat an' play owre the green and grassy haugh, An' in wayward gambols stray doon the burn beside the saugh;"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
